  "$comment": "Path → risk-tier rules read by .claude/scripts/risk-tier.py for a predicted file set (design.md) and for the diff. This is the GENERIC default the baseline ships; /setup-project is meant to generate a project-specific map from detect-signals.sh and PROJECT_KIND (generation is deferred) — until then, edit this one: add your real auth, money and tenant directories. Each rule: glob (fnmatch-style; `**/` = any depth; a glob with no `/` matches the file name at any depth), tier (T0..T3), signal (a trigger name from .claude/templates/governance/tiers.json), why. Every matching rule fires; the highest tier wins, and a rule can only raise a tier. Two rules are CANDIDATES at T2 whose content decides more: a migration file is T3 when it alters, drops, renames or updates an existing table (risk-tier.py reads it), and an API contract file is a breaking-api candidate a reviewer confirms. Manifest rules (signal new-dependency) fire on a diff only when the diff ADDS a dependency line. JSON, not YAML (D1): the standard library parses JSON, and a hand-rolled YAML subset fails silently.",
